      "repository": "openssl/openssl",
      "url": "https://github.com/openssl/openssl",
      "trending_rank": 15,
      "description": "The ==general-purpose TLS and cryptography library== behind a large share of the internet's encrypted connections, with the openssl command-line tool. Feature release OpenSSL 4.1.0 was published on 23 October.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. 4.1.0 ==adds DTLS 1.3 (RFC 9147)==, the datagram version of TLS 1.3 used over UDP, plus RFC 8701 GREASE, DTLS in the SSL listener API and an IKEv2 KDF. It also brings optimised post-quantum ML-DSA and ML-KEM code on ppc64le and x86_64 and drops the Windows-on-Itanium and Windows CE targets.",
      "caveat": "The release lists ==a known DTLS 1.3 issue==: after a KeyUpdate, other post-handshake records awaiting acknowledgement (such as a NewSessionTicket) are no longer retransmitted. Build options changed too (no-ecdsa and no-ecdh are gone; use no-ec), and tsget now needs a different Perl module. Most people get OpenSSL from their OS vendor, so the version you run depends on your distribution. Speed-up claims are the project's own.",
      "category": "Security / cryptography library",
