      "trending_rank": 1,
      "description": "A ==high-performance, multiplayer code editor== written in Rust by the creators of Atom and Tree-sitter, available for macOS, Linux and Windows, with a built-in AI agent panel and Git tools. Version 1.27.0 was published on 4 November; today it tops GitHub's list.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Zed ships weekly, and 1.27.0 targets the cost of AI features: the ==agent panel now loads tool-call diffs and Markdown only when viewed==, cutting memory, CPU and disk reads on long threads (the project's description). AI commit messages now copy the style of the repository's three most recent commits, and Go 1.27 generic methods get syntax highlighting.",
      "caveat": "Performance improvements are the maintainers' own description, not measured here. AI features send code and context to whichever model provider you configure, so check what leaves your machine. The source is ==mainly GPL-3.0-or-later, with Apache-2.0 components where marked==, which matters if you fork or embed it. There is no web version yet.",
