      "description": "The ==open-source monitoring system and time-series database== that scrapes metrics, stores them locally and answers PromQL queries, with alerting rules. A Cloud Native Computing Foundation project. Version 3.16.0 was published on 5 November.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. 3.16.0 adds ==experimental query cost estimation, cost reporting and execution limits== (behind --enable-feature=query-cost), a guard against expensive queries that can stall a server. Smoothed and anchored vector selectors become stable, an experimental integral() function arrives, and Agent mode gains metadata WAL records.",
      "caveat": "The cost features and integral() are experimental and off by default. The release also ==changes behaviour==: the default external URL becomes https when TLS is configured, some deprecated remote-write metrics disappear, and exemplars with duplicate label names are now rejected. Dashboards and alerts that rely on those metrics need checking before upgrading.",
