      "repository": "astral-sh/ruff",
      "url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff",
      "trending_rank": 18,
      "description": "A ==Python linter and code formatter written in Rust== that covers rules from Flake8 and its plugins, isort and others and formats code in a Black-compatible style, as one command-line tool. Version 0.17.4 was published on 5 November.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Ruff is a practical way to replace several Python tools with one. 0.17.4 is a maintenance release: a ==new preview security rule for tarfile ignore_zeros==, safer fixes for logging-format rule G004, a fix for a crash on files that start with a byte-order mark, and a set of formatter and linter performance changes.",
      "caveat": "The ==10-100x speed figure is the maintainers' claim== against Flake8 and Black, not measured here. Ruff is still pre-1.0, so rule behaviour and defaults can change between minor versions; pin the version in CI. The new security rule is a preview rule and is off unless you enable preview mode.",
